<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gokstad ship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 890</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gokstad ship is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> ship of about 890, found in a burial mound at Gokstad near Sandefjord in Vestfold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, and excavated in 1880. About 23 metres long, built of oak with sixteen pairs of oars and a sail, it was seaworthy enough for a replica to cross the Atlantic in 1893. It held the burial of a powerful man and is displayed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gokstad-ship.jpg" alt="Gokstad ship" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karamell · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gokstadskipet1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
